# Normalise line endings.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks every text file out as
# CRLF while the repository stores LF. Biome's formatter expects LF, so any file
# an editor rewrote came back flagged as entirely reformatted — the diff was
# real, but it was pure carriage returns, and it buried actual changes.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` tells Git to store LF and to check LF out on every platform,
# regardless of each developer's `core.autocrlf`. It is the setting the formatter
# already assumes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts genuinely need CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries — Git's heuristic is good but these are worth pinning,
# since a stray newline conversion corrupts them silently.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.node binary
